subproblem.statement:
Let P, q ∈ ℕ, X ∈ 𝒟_{q+1}(ℝ^P) with spt X compact, and Y ∈ 𝒟_{q+2}(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ (q+1) and (q+1+1)). Let G_i : ℝ^{q+1} → ℝ^P (i ∈ ℕ) be Lipschitz, A_i ⊆ ℝ^{q+1} Borel, and w_i : ℝ^{q+1} → ℤ and c_i : ℝ^{q+1} → ℝ measurable. Assume:
- G_i is differentiable at every point of A_i, and G_i(A_i) ⊆ spt X;
- w_i is integrable on A_i;
- for u ∈ A_i, c_i(u) ≥ 0 and |α(DG_i(u)e)| ≤ c_i(u)|α| for all (q+1)-covectors α (|α| = covectorEuclideanNorm α);
- Σ_i ∫⁻_{A_i} |w_i| c_i < ∞;
- X(γ) = Σ_i ∫_{A_i} w_i(u) γ(G_i u)(DG_i(u)e) du (HasSum) for every γ ∈ 𝒟^{q+1}(ℝ^P);
- for every ω ∈ 𝒟^{q+2}(ℝ^P) there is η ∈ 𝒟^{q+1}(ℝ^P) with η(x) = ∫_0^1 t^{q+1} ι_x(ω(t x)) dt for x ∈ spt X and Y(ω) = X(η).
Then there are, for i ∈ ℕ, Lipschitz H_i : ℝ^{q+2} → ℝ^P, Borel B_i ⊆ ℝ^{q+2}, and measurable h_i : ℝ^{q+2} → ℤ and c′_i : ℝ^{q+2} → ℝ such that:
- h_i is integrable on B_i;
- for w ∈ B_i, c′_i(w) ≥ 0 and |α(DH_i(w)e_0, …, DH_i(w)e_{q+1})| ≤ c′_i(w)|α| for all (q+2)-covectors α;
- Σ_i ∫⁻_{B_i} |h_i| c′_i < ∞;
- Y(ω) = Σ_i ∫_{B_i} h_i(w) ω(H_i w)(DH_i(w)e) dw (HasSum) for every ω ∈ 𝒟^{q+2}(ℝ^P).
Remark (not part of the Lean statement): the constructed maps satisfy H_i(s, u) = s G_i(u) on (0,1) × A_i, the cone parametrization of step 8 of the parent proof.

Let P, k ∈ ℕ and T ∈ 𝒟_{k+1}(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ (k+1)). Suppose that for i ∈ ℕ there are Lipschitz G_i : ℝ^{k+1} → ℝ^P, Borel A_i ⊆ ℝ^{k+1}, and measurable w_i : ℝ^{k+1} → ℤ and c_i : ℝ^{k+1} → ℝ such that:
- w_i is integrable on A_i;
- for u ∈ A_i, c_i(u) ≥ 0 and |α(DG_i(u)e_0, …, DG_i(u)e_k)| ≤ c_i(u)·|α| for all (k+1)-covectors α (|α| = covectorEuclideanNorm α);
- Σ_i ∫⁻_{A_i} |w_i|·c_i < ∞;
- for every ω ∈ 𝒟^{k+1}(ℝ^P), Σ_i ∫_{A_i} w_i(u)·ω(G_i(u))(DG_i(u)e_0, …, DG_i(u)e_k) du converges to T(ω) (HasSum).
Then T is integer multiplicity. (Simon Ch. 6, 3.10 in the form of step 9 of the parent proof.)

Let P, q ∈ ℕ and X ∈ 𝒟_{q+1}(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ (q+1)) with ∂X = 0 (X.boundary = 0) and spt X compact. Let R = (M, θ, ξ) be an integer multiplicity triple in ℝ^P (IMRep univ (q+1)) representing X, with M ⊆ spt X and μ_R(ℝ^P) = ∫_M θ dH^{q+1} < ∞ (R.measure univ ≠ ∞).
Then there is Y ∈ 𝒟_{q+2}(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ (q+1+1)) such that:
- ∂Y = X;
- spt Y is compact and spt Y ⊆ C₀ := {s x : s ∈ [0,1], x ∈ spt X};
- for every ω ∈ 𝒟^{q+2}(ℝ^P) there is η ∈ 𝒟^{q+1}(ℝ^P) with η(x) = ∫_0^1 t^{q+1}·ι_x(ω(t x)) dt for every x ∈ spt X and Y(ω) = X(η) (ι_xα = α.curryLeft x).
Y is the cone 0 ⨯ X of Simon Ch. 6, 2.26 (steps 0 and 3–6 of the parent proof).
